# Variant proof battle 1 of 6 — the Warden (docs/ENEMY_ROSTER.md).

id: nv-01-the-toll
number: 701
name: The Toll
pool: Ordinary
description: A Warden plugs the only gap in the wall. It never moves, so the door stays shut until you push it, pull it, or pay for it.
design: The question: what do you do about a thing that will not move?
design: Player A is bottled behind a wall with exactly one way out, and a Warden is standing in it. Move 0 means the planner never even looks for a tile to walk to: its intent is Hold in round 1, Hold in round 2, and Hold in round 6. Every other enemy on this board closes; this one does not. Two counterplays are live on row 3 and both use the stat block honestly.
design: Bull Rush is Push 2, and push resistance 1 turns that into exactly 1 tile. The door opens.
design: Reel is a Pull, and push resistance never reads a Pull. Player B can drag it clear from the far side.
design: Paying the toll is the third option: 12 HP and 4 damage a round to whoever stands next to it.
retired: bestiary fixtures, not designs — the enemies they prove are redeployed into the curated set

spawn w = Warden
spawn l = Lobber
spawn h = Husk

roster a: Vanguard, Archer
roster b: Threadcaster, Wardbearer

board:
  .#.l..B
  .#..H.B
  .#...HB
  .w.....
  A#.....
  A#...^.
  A#.h.^.
